From 60c2e0be428c7df8ff5528cca778febb768eca46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Schuldesz <paulschuldesz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:29:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH milos-linux v1 2/3] media: qcom: camss: csid-340: Use a
 three-bit PHY select field
To: Jorijn van der Graaf <jorijnvdgraaf@catcrafts.net>

CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL is programmed with the CSIPHY index plus
CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_BASE_IDX (1). The mask is GENMASK(21, 20), which
is enough for the two CSIPHYs of QCM2290 but not for Milos, which also
uses csid_ops_340 and has CSIPHY3: 3 + 1 = 4 is truncated to 0, so the
CSID listens to no PHY at all.

The downstream register map for this CSID (csid665 in the Fairphone
camera-kernel) defines the field as three bits (mask 0x7). Widen the
mask to GENMASK(22, 20). The encodings for PHY0..PHY2 do not change.

Fixes the Fairphone 6 front camera (S5KKD1 on CSIPHY3) delivering no
frames.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
index 9a5a6710c0c6..689a76935b1f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 #define CSID_CSI2_RX_CFG0					(0x100)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_NUM_ACTIVE_LANES_MASK	GENMASK(1, 0)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_DLX_INPUT_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(17, 4)
-#define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(21, 20)
+#define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(22, 20)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_BASE_IDX	1
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_TYPE_SEL		BIT(24)
 
-- 
2.54.0

